:: D00_Morning [nobr]
<<set $day to 0>>
<<set $timeslot to "Morning">>
<<set $weekDay to "Thursday">>
<<HUD>>

<<SceneDivider "Thursday Morning, 6:45 AM">>

<<ImagePlaceholder "POV from the mattress, water-stained ceiling, grey dawn light, cracked phone alarm" "banner" "assets/locations/apartment/d00-morning-pov.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>The alarm screams at 6:45 like it always does, that default iPhone tone I&apos;ve come to associate with the exact flavor of dread that comes with being alive. I reach for the phone without opening my eyes, thumb sliding across the cracked screen to kill it. Snooze. Nine more minutes of not existing.</p>

<p>I hit snooze again at 6:54.</p>

<p>At 7:03 I finally peel my eyes open and stare at the ceiling. There&apos;s a water stain directly above my mattress, brown and vaguely fist-shaped, that&apos;s been there since I moved in eight months ago. I&apos;ve thought about complaining to Mrs. Park, my landlord, but Mrs. Park is a five-foot-one Korean-American woman in her sixties who already thinks I&apos;m a deadbeat, and I&apos;m two months behind on rent, so the stain stays. Everything stays. That&apos;s the thing about being broke, nothing ever changes because change costs money.</p>

<p>I sit up. The mattress sits right on the floor because a bed frame was eighty dollars I didn&apos;t have when I moved in and still don&apos;t have now. The sheets are grey, originally white, but a load of laundry costs three fifty and I space it out as long as I can. My studio is exactly what you&apos;d expect for six hundred fifty a month in a neighborhood that calls itself &quot;up and coming&quot; the way a boxer calls himself &quot;getting back up&quot; between rounds, half-heartedly, mostly just to get hit again.</p>

<p>One room split into the illusion of several. A mattress in the corner, a kitchenette against the far wall, a bathroom door that barely clears the toilet when it swings open. Home, such as it is.</p>

</div>

<div class="choice-block">
	<<link '<span>Get up and see what the day wants from you</span>' "Home">><</link>>
</div>
